  "source": "Schneider Electric Modbus Registers Map - Conext CL Three Phase PV Inverter 20/25kVA, doc. 503-0243-01-01 rev. 1.5 (2016-03-15)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Modbus Registers Map - Conext CL Three Phase PV Inverter 20/25kVA (applicable to both NA and IEC models)",
      "version": "503-0243-01-01 rev. 1.5",
      "date": "2016-03-15",
      "url": "https://solar.se.com/au/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2021/11/Conext-CL_Modbus-Registers-Map_Rev1.5.pdf",
      "note": "sections 2-4"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Covers the Conext CL-E (PVSCL20E, PVSCL25E) and CL-NA (PVSCL18NA, PVSCL25NA) inverters; the file keeps its old name.",
    "Modbus RTU defaults: address 10, 9600 bit/s, no parity, 1 stop bit (parity and stop bits can also be even/odd and 2). Modbus TCP: port 502, unit ID 10.",
    "Functions 03, 06, 16 and 43 (device identification). Addresses are 0-based (on the wire). Unused addresses read 0xFF without an exception.",
    "32-bit values are high word first. Strings are null-terminated ASCII; unused characters read 0xFF.",
    "The reactive power control registers apply to the E (IEC) models only. Registers the map marks 'not available' (rated powers, LVRT, P(f), anti-islanding) are left out.",
    "The SunSpec block starts at 40000 (0x9C40): common model 1, three-phase inverter model 103 and multiple MPPT model 160, ending at 0x9CEC.",
    "The register map carries a confidentiality notice, but Schneider Electric publishes it on its solar website.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's register map; not tested on a device."
  ],
